-- title:
--   Transversal index-ℓ² ideals come from norm-ℓ elements
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N, q, q'$ with $N \neq 0$ and $q, q'$ prime, assume $q \nmid N$, $q' \nmid N$ and $q' \neq q$, and let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` holds for the quaternion algebra $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the algebra $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda \subset B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, meaning it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among such orders containing it. Let $N$ be squarefree and let $R \subset B$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, an intersection $\Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1 : R] = N$, with $R \le \Lambda$. Let $J' \subset B$ satisfy: $\Lambda \le J'$; $\Lambda J' \subseteq J'$; $N y \in \Lambda$ for all $y \in J'$; the index of $\Lambda$ in $J'$ is $N^2$; and, for $x \in \Lambda$, $x \in R$ if and only if $y x \in J'$ for all $y \in J'$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \neq q'$, and let $J \subset B$ satisfy $J \le \Lambda$, $\ell \Lambda \subseteq J$, $\Lambda J \subseteq J$, the index of $J$ in $\Lambda$ being $\ell^2$, and the transversality condition that $y \in J'$ with $\ell y \in J$ forces $y \in \Lambda$. The conclusion is the existence of $t \in R$ with $\operatorname{nrd} t = \ell$ (where $\operatorname{nrd} x = x_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a\, x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2 - b\, x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2 + ab\, x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$) such that $J = \Lambda t$ and $\ell J' + \Lambda t = J' t$, both equalities stated elementwise.
--
--   This is the algebra-side input for the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$ on a quaternionic curve of level $N$ ($T_\ell$ when $\ell \nmid N$, $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$): left $\Lambda$-ideals of index $\ell^2$ that are transversal to the level module $J'$ are precisely those generated by an element of reduced norm $\ell$ of the Eichler order, and such a generator transports the level module. It is cited by [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_nrd_eq_levelIdentity_and_forall_exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_mul_mul_iff_of_levelIdentity`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_nrd_eq_levelIdentity_and_forall_exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_mul_mul_iff_of_levelIdentity) and [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.forall_le_qmPeriodLattice_transversal_iff_exists_mem_nrd_eq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.forall_le_qmPeriodLattice_transversal_iff_exists_mem_nrd_eq).
